course: dictionary
lesson: 7559
title: Preparation: getting ready
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Preparation is a noun, and it means getting ready for something, or making something ready. «Preparation is half the work.» This tells you that getting ready properly takes a lot of effort, about as much as the job itself.
explain: Preparations, in the plural, means the many things you do to get ready for an event. «Make preparations» or «preparations for the school play» means all the jobs before the show starts, like learning lines, making costumes and checking the stage.
explain: A preparation can also be a mixture made for a use, such as a medicine or a cream. Context tells you which meaning you need: if the sentence is about a trip or a test, it means getting ready; if it is about a tube or a bottle, it probably means a mixture.
fact: Preparation means getting ready for something, or making something ready.
fact: Preparations means the things you do to get ready for an event.
fact: A preparation is a mixture made for a use, like a medicine or cream.
fact: «In preparation for» means getting ready for something, as in «in preparation for the test».
fact: Preparation time is the time needed to get food ready before cooking, as written on a recipe.
exercise: «Preparation is half the work.» What does preparation mean here? | A mixture for a sore knee | A loud noise | *Getting ready for something | Finishing the job
exercise: The school trip is next week, so the teachers make preparations. What are preparations? | A mixture for a cough | *The jobs done to get ready for the trip | A kind of bus | The trip itself, after it has finished
exercise: On a recipe card you read «preparation time: 15 minutes». What does preparation time mean? | The time you spend eating | The time the cake spends in the oven | The time the shop is open | *The time needed to get the food ready before cooking
test: «The nurse gave him a cream, a preparation for his rash.» What is a preparation here? | A plan for a party | A school test | A long walk | *A mixture made for a use, like a cream
test: Which phrase shows getting ready for a school play? | Make a wish | Preparation time | *In preparation for the play | At the end of the day
exam: What does «Preparation is half the work» tell you? | Only half the work needs doing | *Getting ready takes about as much effort as the job itself | Preparation is a kind of medicine | Work is more fun than preparation
